27. Qb4! { [%cal Gb4f4] } (27. Qc4? Bxd5 $10) (27. Bxc6? bxc6 28. Qa4 c5 $10) 27... Bxd5 (27... Be5 28. Qxf4 Bxf4 29. Bxg7+ $18) 28. Bxd4! { The right capture, as Black's queen is a target! } { [%csl Rf4][%cal Gd4g7,Rb4f4] } 28... Rf6! { Stockfish doesn't like it, but this move forces White to find the only winning move! } 29. Rxg7!! { [%anno "AAArmstark", aaarmstark] Otherwise, Black was threatening to begin his own attack with ♗xg2! } { [%csl Rg2][%cal Rd5g2,Gg7g2] } 29... Rg8 { White has one more problem to solve! } 30. Bxf6! { A neat finish, but not the only one. } (30. Rg3! { was also winning. }) 30... Qxb4 { Now White has many moves to win, but our task is to find the mate in 3! } 31. Rf7+! { The fastest way to win! Black resigned, since it's a mate in 3. } 31... Rg7 32. Re8+ Kh7 33. Rxg7# { [%anno "AAArmstark", aaarmstark] Replay the game: https://lichess.org/broadcast/46th-fide-chess-olympiad-samarkand-2026-open-matches-13-37/round-1/aJJ3Lq0n/AzkU37YC } 1-0


